getExportedServices [SimTalk]
Returns all services which the Exporter/Worker designated by <Path> exports at the moment.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getExportedServices([Services:table]) -> any
Parameter
The optional parameter Services of data type table designates the name of the table into which Plant
Simulation writes the services.
The table has one column. It contains all services that the Exporter/Worker exports at the moment. The
subtable contains all importers importing that service and the number of services which the Exporter
provides for the importer (integer).
Return Value
The return value is an array containing the services which the Exporter/Worker currently exports if you do
not specify the optional parameter.
Example
MyExporter.getExportedServices(MyExportedServicesTable)
MyExporter.getExportedServices         // returns an array
print MyExporter.getExportedServices   // might return [Job1]
See also
Services [SimTalk] - Exporter
